# Factory source in a consumer repository

This directory contains the factory package subset delivered by the Adaptive Grok Build consumer installer. Begin with the consumer's [engineering contract](../AGENTS.md) and [adaptive delivery workflow](../.agents/skills/adaptive-delivery/SKILL.md). Installation supplies source and local workflow tools; it does not start a service, provision a database, enable a provider or publish a site.

## Installed files

- [Python package](src/adaptive_factory/) and its [packaged migrations](src/adaptive_factory/resources/).
- [API and event contracts](contracts/), including the [control API](contracts/openapi/factory-control.v1.json) and [execution API](contracts/openapi/factory-execution.v1.json).
- [Package metadata](pyproject.toml), [dependency lock](uv.lock), [Compose definition](compose.yaml), and placeholder [actor configuration](actors.example.json).
- [Selected package tests](tests/), including the [disposable database test runner](tests/run_disposable_exit.py). This is a selected test subset, not the full upstream test suite.
- Repository-level [route](../scripts/grok_route.py), [status](../scripts/grok_status.py), [verification](../scripts/grok_verify.py) and [doctor](../scripts/grok_doctor.py) commands.

Run consumer workflow commands from the repository root. Use the active route's verification profiles and preserve its exact evidence requirements. Local verification is workflow evidence; merging still requires the consumer's externally configured checks and approvals on the exact pull-request head.

The installer retains this README as a managed file. Existing-target installation emits a read-only plan; it does not update this file or the managed AGENTS block. Applying an update requires a separately reviewed consumer change that preserves user-owned text outside the managed markers and honors declared `kept_local` ownership. New-target materialization requires an absent target.

